анный) и запрещены во время Песаха по еврейскому закону.. Однако, киноа должна быть сертифицирована как «Кошерная для Песаха» из-за потенциального перекрестного загрязнения..</p><p data-start="432" data-end="548">Но что такое хамец? Почему киноа освобождена от налога? <span class ="tr_" id="tr_12" data-source="" data-orig="And how is quinoa used during Passover and beyond">And how is quinoa used during Passover and beyond</span>? <span class ="tr_" id="tr_13" data-source="" data-orig="Let’s explore">Let’s explore</span>.</p><hr data-start="550" data-end="553" /><h2 data-start="555" data-end="577"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="What_Is_Chametz"></span><span class ="tr_" id="tr_14" data-source="" data-orig="What Is Chametz">What Is Chametz</span>?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="579" data-end="766"><strong data-start="579" data-end="590"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_15" data-source="" data-orig="Chametz">Chametz</span></strong> (<span class ="tr_" id="tr_16" data-source="" data-orig="חָמֵץ">חָמֵץ</span>) <span class ="tr_" id="tr_17" data-source="" data-orig="refers to any food product made from five specific grains that has come into contact with water and been allowed to ferment for more than">refers to any food product made from five specific grains that has come into contact with water and been allowed to ferment for more than</span> 18 <span class ="tr_" id="tr_18" data-source="" data-orig="minutes">minutes</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_19" data-source="" data-orig="These grains are">These grains are</span>:</p><ul data-start="768" data-end="815"><li data-start="768" data-end="777"><p data-start="770" data-end="777"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_20" data-source="" data-orig="Wheat">Wheat</span></p></li><li data-start="778" data-end="788"><p data-start="780" data-end="788"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_21" data-source="" data-orig="Barley">Barley</span></p></li><li data-start="789" data-end="796"><p data-start="791" data-end="796"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_22" data-source="" data-orig="Rye">Rye</span></p></li><li data-start="797" data-end="805"><p data-start="799" data-end="805">Овес</p></li><li data-start="806" data-end="815"><p data-start="808" data-end="815"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_23" data-source="" data-orig="Spelt">Spelt</span></p></li></ul><p data-start="817" data-end="1030"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_24" data-source="" data-orig="Anything leavened from these grains is forbidden during">Anything leavened from these grains is forbidden during</span> <strong data-start="873" data-end="894"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_25" data-source="" data-orig="Passover">Passover</span> (Песах)</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_26" data-source="" data-orig="according to Halacha">according to Halacha</span> (<span class ="tr_" id="tr_27" data-source="" data-orig="Jewish law">Jewish law</span>). <span class ="tr_" id="tr_28" data-source="" data-orig="This includes bread">This includes bread</span>, макароны, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_29" data-source="" data-orig="cereal">cereal</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_30" data-source="" data-orig="and many processed foods unless they are certified for Passover">and many processed foods unless they are certified for Passover</span>.</p><hr data-start="1032" data-end="1035" /><h2 data-start="1037" data-end="1068"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Why_Quinoa_Is_Not_Chametz"></span><span class ="tr_" id="tr_31" data-source="" data-orig="Why Quinoa Is Not Chametz">Why Quinoa Is Not Chametz</span><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="1070" data-end="1264"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_32" data-source="" data-orig="Quinoa">Quinoa</span> (<span class ="tr_" id="tr_33" data-source="" data-orig="Chenopodium quinoa">Chenopodium quinoa</span>) <span class ="tr_" id="tr_34" data-source="" data-orig="is botanically not a grain at all">is botanically not a grain at all</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_35" data-source="" data-orig="It’s a">It’s a</span> <strong data-start="1140" data-end="1157"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_36" data-source="" data-orig="pseudo-cereal">pseudo-cereal</span></strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_37" data-source="" data-orig="from South America">from South America</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_38" data-source="" data-orig="belonging to the">belonging to the</span> <strong data-start="1195" data-end="1214"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_39" data-source="" data-orig="amaranth family">amaranth family</span></strong>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_40" data-source="" data-orig="and unrelated to wheat and other chametz grains">and unrelated to wheat and other chametz grains</span>.</p><h3 data-start="1266" data-end="1304"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Key_Reasons_Quinoa_Is_Not_Chametz"></span><span class ="tr_" id="tr_41" data-source="" data-orig="Key Reasons Quinoa Is Not Chametz">Key Reasons Quinoa Is Not Chametz</span>:<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="1306" data-end="1476"><li data-start="1306" data-end="1346"><p data-start="1308" data-end="1346"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_42" data-source="" data-orig="❌ Not one of the five chametz grains">❌ Not one of the five chametz grains</span></p></li><li data-start="1347" data-end="1401"><p data-start="1349" data-end="1401"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_43" data-source="" data-orig="❌ Does not ferment naturally when mixed with water">❌ Does not ferment naturally when mixed with water</span></p></li><li data-start="1402" data-end="1429"><p data-start="1404" data-end="1429"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_44" data-source="" data-orig="✅ Naturally gluten-free">✅ Naturally gluten-free</span></p></li><li data-start="1430" data-end="1476"><p data-start="1432" data-end="1476"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_45" data-source="" data-orig="✅ Considered kosher when properly supervised">✅ Considered kosher when properly supervised</span></p></li></ul><blockquote data-start="1478" data-end="1841"><p data-start="1480" data-end="1506"><strong data-start="1480" data-end="1505">